        "created_at": "2021-06-07T17:21:12.586Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Cult_of_Gloom\" data-post=\"7\" data-topic=\"28524\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cult_of_gloom/48/1878_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Cult_of_Gloom:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My reading has been that a mod apply to an effect die, and all effects that are tied to that particular die are modified. So you would split them up between your Max die, your Mid die, and your Min die before you roll.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That is what the rules say, taken literally: they affect an effect die.  However, the question has been asked on The Letters Page, and the ruling was that each mod applies to a specific effect, not the entire die.  So if you use some Mid-based ability with a +2, plus Inspiring Totem, and incur a twist using your Mid die, that +2 would not apply to Inspiring Totem and the twist.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-06-07T17:21:34.170Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
